with the following attributes.\n1043 | \n1044 |         data : {ndarray, dataframe} of shape (20, 3)\n1045 |             The data matrix. If `as_frame=True`, `data` will be a pandas\n1046 |             DataFrame.\n1047 |         target: {ndarray, dataframe} of shape (20, 3)\n1048 |             The regression targets. If `as_frame=True`, `target` will be\n1049 |             a pandas DataFrame.\n1050 |         feature_names: list\n1051 |             The names of the dataset columns.\n1052 |         target_names: list\n1053 |             The names of the target columns.\n1054 |         frame: DataFrame of shape (20, 6)\n1055 |             Only present when `as_frame=True`. DataFrame with `data` and\n1056 |             `target`.\n1057 | \n1058 |             .. versionadded:: 0.23\n1059 |         DESCR: str\n1060 |             The full description of the dataset.\n1061 |         data_filename: str\n1062 |             The path to the location of the data.\n1063 |         target_filename: str\n1064 |             The path to the location of the target.\n1065 | \n1066 |             .. versionadded:: 0.20\n1067 | \n1068 |     (data, target) : tuple if ``return_X_y`` is True\n1069 | \n1070 |         .. versionadded:: 0.18\n1071 |     \"\"\"\n1072 |     data_filename = \"linnerud_exercise.csv\"\n1073 |     target_filename = \"linnerud_physiological.csv\"\n1074 | \n1075 |     # Read header and data\n1076 |     with resources.open_text(DATA_MODULE, data_filename) as f:\n1077 |         header_exercise = f.readline().split()\n1078 |         f.seek(0)  # reset file obj\n1079 |         data_exercise = np.loadtxt(f, skiprows=1)\n1080 | \n1081 |     with resources.open_text(DATA_MODULE, target_filename) as f:\n1082 |         header_physiological = f.readline().split()\n1083 |         f.seek(0)  # reset file obj\n1084 |         data_physiological = np.loadtxt(f, skiprows=1)\n1085 | \n1086 |     fdescr = load_descr(\"linnerud.rst\")\n1087 | \n1088 |     frame = None\n1089 |     if as_fra