ots of a DataFrame.\n1558 | \n1559 |         Examples\n1560 |         --------\n1561 |         In the example below we have a DataFrame with the information about\n1562 |         planet's mass and radius. We pass the 'mass' column to the\n1563 |         pie function to get a pie plot.\n1564 | \n1565 |         .. plot::\n1566 |             :context: close-figs\n1567 | \n1568 |             >>> df = pd.DataFrame({'mass': [0.330, 4.87 , 5.97],\n1569 |             ...                    'radius': [2439.7, 6051.8, 6378.1]},\n1570 |             ...                   index=['Mercury', 'Venus', 'Earth'])\n1571 |             >>> plot = df.plot.pie(y='mass', figsize=(5, 5))\n1572 | \n1573 |         .. plot::\n1574 |             :context: close-figs\n1575 | \n1576 |             >>> plot = df.plot.pie(subplots=True, figsize=(11, 6))\n1577 |         \"\"\"\n1578 |         if (\n1579 |             isinstance(self._parent, ABCDataFrame)\n1580 |             and kwargs.get(\"y\", None) is None\n1581 |             and not kwargs.get(\"subplots\", False)\n1582 |         ):\n1583 |             raise ValueError(\"pie requires either y column or 'subplots=True'\")\n1584 |         return self(kind=\"pie\", **kwargs)\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/plotting/__init__.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/plotting/__init__.py` for the full content if needed.\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"DataFrame.plot\", \"DataFrame.plot plot.subplots\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `pandas/plotting/_core.py:PlotAccessor.bar`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n1121 | def bar(self, x=None, y=None, **kwargs):\n1122 |         \"\"\"\n1123 |         Vertical bar plot.\n1124 | \n1125 |         A bar plot is a plot that presents categorical data with\n1126 |         rectangular bars with lengths proportional to the values that they\n1127 |         represent. A bar plot shows comparisons among discrete categories. One\n1128 |         a