irs are given, the mapping is from *value*\n1094 |             to *color*. This can be used to divide the range unevenly.\n1095 |         N : int\n1096 |             The number of RGB quantization levels.\n1097 |         gamma : float\n1098 |         \"\"\"\n1099 |         if not np.iterable(colors):\n1100 |             raise ValueError('colors must be iterable')\n1101 | \n1102 |         if (isinstance(colors[0], Sized) and len(colors[0]) == 2\n1103 |                 and not isinstance(colors[0], str)):\n1104 |             # List of value, color pairs\n1105 |             vals, colors = zip(*colors)\n1106 |         else:\n1107 |             vals = np.linspace(0, 1, len(colors))\n1108 | \n1109 |         r, g, b, a = to_rgba_array(colors).T\n1110 |         cdict = {\n1111 |             \"red\": np.column_stack([vals, r, r]),\n1112 |             \"green\": np.column_stack([vals, g, g]),\n1113 |             \"blue\": np.column_stack([vals, b, b]),\n1114 |             \"alpha\": np.column_stack([vals, a, a]),\n1115 |         }\n1116 | \n1117 |         return LinearSegmentedColormap(name, cdict, N, gamma)\n```\n\n\n\n##Searching for term \"facecolor\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound function `lib/matplotlib/animation.py:Animation.save`.\nSource: Retrieved code content using keyword search (bm25).\n```\n 936 | def save(self, filename, writer=None, fps=None, dpi=None, codec=None,\n 937 |              bitrate=None, extra_args=None, metadata=None, extra_anim=None,\n 938 |              savefig_kwargs=None, *, progress_callback=None):\n 939 |         \"\"\"\n 940 |         Save the animation as a movie file by drawing every frame.\n 941 | \n 942 |         Parameters\n 943 |         ----------\n 944 |         filename : str\n 945 |             The output filename, e.g., :file:`mymovie.mp4`.\n 946 | \n 947 |         writer : `MovieWriter` or str, default: :rc:`animation.writer`\n 948 |             A `MovieWriter` instance to use or a key that identifies a\n 949 |             class t