ence\n 984 |             between the frames from the different animations.\n 985 | \n 986 |         savefig_kwargs : dict, default: {}\n 987 |             Keyword arguments passed to each `~.Figure.savefig` call used to\n 988 |             save the individual frames.\n 989 | \n 990 |         progress_callback : function, optional\n 991 |             A callback function that will be called for every frame to notify\n 992 |             the saving progress. It must have the signature ::\n 993 | \n 994 |                 def func(current_frame: int, total_frames: int) -> Any\n 995 | \n 996 |             where *current_frame* is the current frame number and *total_frames* is the\n 997 |             total number of frames to be saved. *total_frames* is set to None, if the\n 998 |             total number of frames cannot be determined. Return values may exist but are\n 999 |             ignored.\n1000 | \n1001 |             Example code to write the progress to stdout::\n1002 | \n1003 |                 progress_callback = lambda i, n: print(f'Saving frame {i}/{n}')\n1004 | \n1005 |         Notes\n1006 |         -----\n1007 |         *fps*, *codec*, *bitrate*, *extra_args* and *metadata* are used to\n1008 |         construct a `.MovieWriter` instance and can only be passed if\n1009 |         *writer* is a string.  If they are passed as non-*None* and *writer*\n1010 |         is a `.MovieWriter`, a `RuntimeError` will be raised.\n1011 |         \"\"\"\n1012 | \n1013 |         all_anim = [self]\n1014 |         if extra_anim is not None:\n1015 |             all_anim.extend(anim for anim in extra_anim\n1016 |                             if anim._fig is self._fig)\n1017 | \n1018 |         # Disable \"Animation was deleted without rendering\" warning.\n1019 |         for anim in all_anim:\n1020 |             anim._draw_was_started = True\n1021 | \n1022 |         if writer is None:\n1023 |             writer = mpl.rcParams['animation.writer']\n1024 |         elif (not isinstance(w