l values, pandas rounds\n2489 |         to the nearest even value (e.g. -0.5 and 0.5 round to 0.0, 1.5 and 2.5\n2490 |         round to 2.0, etc.).\n2491 | \n2492 |         Examples\n2493 |         --------\n2494 |         >>> s = pd.Series([-0.5, 0.1, 2.5, 1.3, 2.7])\n2495 |         >>> s.round()\n2496 |         0   -0.0\n2497 |         1    0.0\n2498 |         2    2.0\n2499 |         3    1.0\n2500 |         4    3.0\n2501 |         dtype: float64\n2502 |         \"\"\"\n2503 |         nv.validate_round(args, kwargs)\n2504 |         new_mgr = self._mgr.round(decimals=decimals)\n2505 |         return self._constructor_from_mgr(new_mgr, axes=new_mgr.axes).__finalize__(\n2506 |             self, method=\"round\"\n2507 |         )\n```\n"}, {"content": "Let me also search for the datetime-related rounding functionality:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['pandas/core/accessor.py', 'CombinedDatetimelikeProperties']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"pandas/core/accessor.py\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound file `pandas/core/accessor.py`.\nSource: Exact match found for entity name `pandas/core/accessor.py`.\n```\n  1 | \"\"\"\n  2 | \n  3 | accessor.py contains base classes for implementing accessor properties\n  4 | that can be mixed into or pinned onto other pandas classes.\n  5 | \n  6 | \"\"\"\n  7 | \n  8 | from __future__ import annotations\n  9 | \n 10 | import functools\n 11 | from typing import (\n 12 |     TYPE_CHECKING,\n 13 |     final,\n 14 | )\n 15 | import warnings\n 16 | \n 17 | from pandas.util._decorators import doc\n 18 | from pandas.util._exceptions import find_stack_level\n 19 | \n 20 | if TYPE_CHECKING:\n 21 |     from collections.abc import Callable\n 22 | \n 23 |     from pandas._typing import TypeT\n 24 | \n 25 |     from pandas import Index\n 26 |    