f = pd.DataFrame({\"A\": [1, 1, 1]})\n611 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"background-color: blueGreenRed;\").to_excel(\n612 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n613 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n614 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n615 |     >>> df.style.map(lambda x: \"border: 1px solid red red;\").to_excel(\n616 |     ...     \"styled.xlsx\"\n617 |     ... )  # doctest: +SKIP\n618 |     CSSWarning: Unhandled color format: 'blueGreenRed'\n619 |     \"\"\"\n```\n\nFound file `pandas/core/interchange/dataframe.py`.\nSource: Retrieved entity using keyword search (bm25).\nHint: Search `pandas/core/interchange/dataframe.py` for the full content if needed.\n"}, {"content": "Let me also check the ExcelFormatter class since it's involved in the to_excel functionality:\n\n<function=search_code_snippets>\n<parameter=search_terms>['ExcelFormatter']</parameter>\n", "role": "assistant", "tool_calls": null, "function_call": null}, {"role": "tool", "tool_call_id": "toolu_01", "name": "search_code_snippets", "content": "OBSERVATION:\n##Searching for term \"ExcelFormatter\"...\n### Search Result:\nFound class `pandas/io/formats/excel.py:ExcelFormatter`.\nSource: Match found for entity name `ExcelFormatter`.\nJust show the structure of this class due to response length limitations:\n```\nclass ExcelFormatter:\n\n    max_rows = 2**20\n    max_cols = 2**14\n\n    def __init__(\n        self,\n        df,\n        na_rep: str = \"\",\n        float_format: str | None = None,\n        cols: Sequence[Hashable] | None = None,\n        header: Sequence[Hashable] | bool = True,\n        index: bool = True,\n        index_label: IndexLabel | None = None,\n        merge_cells: ExcelWriterMergeCells = False,\n        inf_rep: str = \"inf\",\n        style_converter: Callable | None = None,\n    ) -> None:\n...\n    def _format_value(self, val):\n...\n    def _format_header_mi(self) -> Iterable[ExcelCell]:\n...\n    def _format_header_regular(self) -> Iterable[ExcelCell]: